---
// Diagram: tier and effort are two independent dials. Left dial = tier
// (fast / everyday / top), right dial = effort (low / high). Static SVG,
// token-driven colours so it re-themes with the page; labels carry the
// meaning so it never relies on colour alone.
---

<figure class="diagram">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 440 240"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="dials-title dials-desc"
    class="diagram__svg"
  >
    <title id="dials-title">Tier and effort are two independent dials</title>
    <desc id="dials-desc">
      Two separate dials side by side. The tier dial sets the model's ceiling
      with three settings - fast, everyday, top. The effort dial sets how hard
      it thinks within that ceiling, from low to high. You turn each one on its
      own.
    </desc>

    {/* Tier dial - stepped, three positions */}
    <g transform="translate(110 120)">
      <circle class="d-face" r="70" />
      {/* tick marks at the three tier positions */}
      <line class="d-tick" x1="0" y1="-70" x2="0" y2="-56" transform="rotate(-55)" />
      <line class="d-tick" x1="0" y1="-70" x2="0" y2="-56" />
      <line class="d-tick" x1="0" y1="-70" x2="0" y2="-56" transform="rotate(55)" />
      {/* pointer set to the middle (everyday) position */}
      <line class="d-pointer" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="-52" />
      <circle class="d-hub" r="7" />
    </g>
    <text class="d-cap" x="110" y="214">TIER</text>
    <text class="d-sub d-sub--l" x="36" y="120">fast</text>
    <text class="d-sub d-sub--t" x="110" y="34">everyday</text>
    <text class="d-sub d-sub--r" x="184" y="120">top</text>

    {/* Effort dial - sweep from low to high */}
    <g transform="translate(330 120)">
      <circle class="d-face" r="70" />
      <line class="d-tick" x1="0" y1="-70" x2="0" y2="-56" transform="rotate(-60)" />
      <line class="d-tick" x1="0" y1="-70" x2="0" y2="-56" transform="rotate(60)" />
      {/* pointer leaning toward high */}
      <line class="d-pointer" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="-52" transform="rotate(38)" />
      <circle class="d-hub" r="7" />
    </g>
    <text class="d-cap" x="330" y="214">EFFORT</text>
    <text class="d-sub d-sub--l" x="256" y="120">low</text>
    <text class="d-sub d-sub--r" x="404" y="120">high</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="diagram__cap">
    Two dials, turned independently: tier sets the ceiling, effort sets how hard
    it works within it.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .diagram {
    margin: var(--space-6) 0;
  }
  .diagram__svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 30rem;
    height: auto;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  .diagram__cap {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    text-align: center;
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .d-face {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 8%, var(--surface));
    stroke: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 40%, var(--border));
    stroke-width: 2;
  }
  .d-tick {
    stroke: var(--muted);
    stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-linecap: round;
  }
  .d-pointer {
    stroke: var(--accent);
    stroke-width: 4;
    stroke-linecap: round;
  }
  .d-hub {
    fill: var(--accent);
  }
  .d-cap {
    fill: var(--text);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-anchor: middle;
  }
  .d-sub {
    fill: var(--muted);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .d-sub--l { text-anchor: end; }
  .d-sub--r { text-anchor: start; }
  .d-sub--t { text-anchor: middle; }
</style>
